{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Oracle-design correction after claim: source inspection of fsck._tracker_sync_status proves a guard-aborted non-fast-forward epoch mismatch is DIVERGED (common ancestor, neither side ancestor), not PUSH_PENDING (remote ancestor and local ahead only). Updated the plan to require DIVERGED, exact ref preservation, and separate sync/push integration ACs; the earlier review-advisory comment's PUSH_PENDING wording is superseded. No production code or tests had been edited."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785814890971356001,"uuid":"86cdbaf3-e1fc-4a2b-bac1-933f58687976"}